{"id": "EUVD-2026-95260", "enisaUuid": "2e468710-962d-397f-ad0d-5aa48f674774", "description": "System Informer before 4.0.26241.138 contains an incorrect authorization vulnerability in the phsvc helper that allows local attackers to reach privileged APIs by connecting from any Authenticode-signed process. Attackers can load code into a Microsoft-signed host like rundll32.exe, connect to SiSvcApiPort, and call PhSvcApiCreateService to execute code as SYSTEM.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T20:15:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T01:19:53", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/winsiderss/systeminformer/commit/ce451a264a424f6f386b1615df651f8364aaeb9f", "https://github.com/winsiderss/systeminformer/blob/v3.2.25011.2103/SystemInformer/phsvc/svcapiport.c#L196-L230", "https://github.com/winsiderss/systeminformer/releases/tag/v4.0.26241.138", "https://github.com/winsiderss/systeminformer", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/system-informer-before-4.0.26241.138-incorrect-authorization-in-phsvc-alpc-port"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mx65-q648-g54f", "CVE-2026-107782"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7441dd40-048e-3a8c-b78f-1c8c809dd6db", "product": {"name": "System Informer", "vendor": {"name": "winsiderss"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.0.26241.138"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "69d15584-b91d-3cd0-9581-b3c2154afcf2", "vendor": {"name": "winsiderss"}}], "isExploited": false}